(registered 2026-10-22, last updated 2026-10-22)

Media type name: application

Media subtype name: vnd.geovirtuallis.geov+zip

Required parameters: N/A

Optional parameters: N/A

Encoding considerations: binary

Inner archive members (project.json, layers/*.geojson) are UTF-8 JSON; the .geov envelope is a ZIP archive.

Security considerations: Data-only ZIP package (UTF-8 JSON + GeoJSON). No executable or active content. Importers should limit ZIP expansion (entry count, size, compression ratio), parse JSON safely, and treat all strings as untrusted. May contain sensitive location/attribute data; protect storage and transport as needed. ZIP decompression risks apply; see RFC 7230 / common ZIP-bomb mitigations. No fragment or external-link interpretation required beyond the published spec.

Interoperability considerations: ZIP is portable across OSes. Inner GeoJSON follows RFC 7946 (lon, lat). JSON is UTF-8. project.json version field defines descriptor semantics; unknown ZIP entries and JSON keys should be ignored.

Published specification:

https://www.gis.com.my/mgs/03-geov-package.html
(Index: https://www.gis.com.my/mgs/
— symbology: https://www.gis.com.my/mgs/02-geov-symbology.html)

Applications which use this media: MiniGISimple (Firefox extension), GISimple, and GeoVirtuallis import/export .geov project packages (vector layers, map view, styles).

Fragment identifier considerations: N/A. This media type does not define fragment identifiers.

Restrictions on usage: None

Additional information:

1. Deprecated alias names for this type: N/A
2. Magic number(s): PK\x03\x04 (ZIP local file header; conventional)
3. File extension(s): .geov
4. Macintosh file type code: GEOV
5. Object Identifiers: N/A

General Comments: Registrant: GIS Innovation Sdn Bhd. Normative spec: https://www.gis.com.my/mgs/03-geov-package.html

